# A module binding created inside module-level control flow — ouroboros#141.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that two walkers disagreed about what a module
# top-level binding IS. `collect_free_assigns`, which builds the rename map,
# walks the whole tree; `module_bindings`, which builds the module's snapshot
# DICT, walked only the immediate statement list. So a binding made inside a
# module-level `if` was spliced and renamed and assigned correctly — and then
# never reached the dict.
#
# The missing key is the visible half; the dangerous half is the second line:
#
#   VM  ["a", "b", "c"]   2          AOT  ["a", "c"]   null
#
# a wrong VALUE, delivered as null into whatever the program does next, with
# rc 0 and a zero-byte build log.
#
# `elif`/`else` and `loop while` bodies are the same shape. A `define` inside
# an `if` refuses loudly instead, so only the value case was silent.

import _q1_mod
print of (keys of _q1_mod)
print of _q1_mod.a
print of _q1_mod.b
print of _q1_mod.c
